/**
 * Flavour text for each card, shown under the standee preview when a card is hovered in the Card Gallery (not in
 * matches). Write each card's text between its double quotes, e.g.
 *   "sentinel_knight": "The wall does not bend.", // Sentinel Knight
 * Apostrophes are fine. A double quote inside the text needs a backslash before it (\"), and \n starts a new line.
 * A card left as "" shows a placeholder for now.
 *
 * Grouped by set, in the same order as the card data. The name after each entry is only a reminder of which card it is.
 * Cards added later can simply be added here by their id.
 */
export const FLAVOUR_TEXT: Record<string, string> = {
  // ---- Realms of Man ----
  "sentinel_knight": "He took and oath to the Order of the Sentinels to protect others. And it's not why he joined, but they give their guys a cool looking brimmed helmet. Seriously guys, he joined because he cares about others. What is he supposed to do, not join because the helmet is too cool?", // Sentinel Knight
  "topaz_mage": "Sometimes, you choose the spark life. Other times, it chooses you. We're not sure which is the case for Topaz Mage, but he can wire both your house or your enemy.", // Topaz Mage
  "duelist_fighter": "After training at the top of mountains and in the rivers beneath obscure valleys, Duelist Fighter pondered whether it is truly the fate of all to stand motionless during the enemy turn.", // Duelist Fighter
  "shade_assassin": "Okay, before inviting this guy to any parties, we need to talk about Shade Step. Holy crap dude, he is going to startle you. Don't even try to anticipate it. Just accept it. You're gonna get startled really bad dude.", // Shade Assassin
  "archivist_sage": "Someone taught this guy to read novels at like age 1 and a half. Holy cow, what a prick. He thinks you need a hard copy of a book to truly get the experience of reading it. Someone get this guy an ebook reader without a backlight, is all I can say.", // Archivist Sage
  "powder_keg_plunderer": "Some men want to see the world burn? I mean sure, but I would argue that's old-gen. We're on explosives now. We like seeing the pieces scatter all over the place rather than just a fire, y'know?", // Powder Keg Plunderer
  "combat_cook": "Don't go to his house after you eat a full-course meal and you're stuffed. This guy gave me a leg of lamb one time at like 9pm. I don't know who does that but it had polenta and gravy and I risked a gut burst for it and it was worth it. Core memory.", // Combat Cook
  "battle_engineer": "You know why they call him the Battle Engineer, right? He usually makes batteries for larger electrical devices to try to speed up scientific progress in the world, but people keep hiring him for easier design work such as building them a more robust wall.", // Battle Engineer
  "conflict_correspondent": "He works for the local news outlet to keep you informed about the things happening in his county. Right now, the realm is at civil war ever since its king was revealed to be a faceless shapeshifter. Nonetheless, the correspondent takes his job seriously.", // Conflict Correspondent
  "happy_camper": "Sometimes, in life, you have to leave the raging to the bonfire and learn to have a good time. There's no fixing the outside world, and as long as we can still grill over the fire and try to forget about it, those people are welcome to have their issues somewhere else.", // Happy Camper
  "imbued_knight": "You never would've honestly seen this guy on a card if they didn't imbue him. Look at this guy. Gem sitting on his armour and shield and stuff. He doesn't have a damn clue. Just plink a rock off this guy's head for me, will you? Just imbuing anybody these days.", // Imbued Knight
  "polearm_knight": "She had a nail to hammer that was really far away at the farmhouse one day, and there was a pile of stuff in the way. I think the rest of the story sort of tells itself. Other knights are so scared of Polearm that most of them don't realize she's a girl.", // Polearm Knight
  "greatsword_knight": "You can't hold a shield AND a sword that big at the same time. Nobody has ever done it. Greatsword Knight made a special effort at the gym to get so big that he could hold a sword big enough to hide behind as compensation. It makes sense if you've ever tried holding a shield with a big sword, trust me.", // Greatsword Knight
  "longbow_knight": "You don't technically have to be a melee specialist to be a knight. Nobody even reads the freaking manual anymore, dude. Just off to war, I guess. Yeah, you get to bring a bow if you have one at home. They just don't make extra ones for you because generally those go to the guys with no armour.", // Longbow Knight
  "bastion_knight": "After a certain number of times trying to hold like 11 guys from getting into the door at once, you've got multiple sets of hands grabbing your weapon, you just don't need all that. Try moving me now, big boy. Or I imagine that's sort of how the sentiment sounded in his head.", // Bastion Knight
  "euclase_mage": "There's this prejudice against people who use ice magic. Euclase has been accused of being unemotional at times, and doesn't really take kindly to it. The irony is, the distance she keeps from others as a result just seems to confirm the way they feel about this.", // Euclase Mage
  "garnet_mage": "Have you ever walked into a room where you and your buddies are fighting half a dozen enemies, you're armpit deep in skeletons and oozes, and all of a sudden some prick fireballs everyone? Well, he's usually on the other end of that one, to be honest.", // Garnet Mage
  "opal_mage": "Reflected in the iridescence of the opal is the fluidity of sea's roiling waters. The Opal Mage, trapped aboard a ship for many months, was once struck by horrible seasickness. By channelling the opal, they found a way to be at peace with the troubled waters through newfound magic.", // Opal Mage
  "dravite_mage": "Some stones appear plainer than others, but beauty is subjective. The Dravite Mage saw in the brown of the stone the same shade as the eyes of someone they once loved, and channeled it for the ability to protect the new people they had come to consider family.", // Dravite Mage
  "amethyst_mage": "The strange purple colour of the amethyst was unlike any hue the mage had seen in her life. With its piercing colour, she imagined, maybe a magician could crumble even the heavy plate armour her captors wore like paper. And her plan prevailed as she escaped those cruel mines once and for all.", // Amethyst Mage
  "halberd_fighter": "The king of weapons and apex of armaments, the halberd reigns supreme on the battlefield. Or so this particular wielder would tell you, and he certainly makes it seem that way. A man this young should not have survived as many battles as he has, but the proof of concept keeps them sending him to the fray.", // Halberd Fighter
  "spear_fighter": "Versatile and adaptable, the Spear Fighter is one of many. Not longing to be unique, he takes pride that his fighting style has seen such success that many take it up. If we've ever invented a better armament than a spear, he might ask, then why don't we seen more soldiers wielding them?", // Spear Fighter
  "crossbow_fighter": "Armed with the latest technology and the skill to use it, the Crossbow Fighter represents a moment in warfare where even the staunchest purists are forced to concede, we need to be prepared. Sharp bolts of wood just didn't used to fly at you quite as fast back in the day.", // Crossbow Fighter
  "dual_sword_fighter": "Look, not everyone can afford to be a knight, okay? Ugh, maybe this guy is a bad example. Yes, he went and bought TWO swords. They're really expensive. But at the end of the day, being a fighter is a mindset. If he were a pansy, then maybe he would've spent the money on armour and fancy schooling. But he isn't.", // Dual-Sword Fighter
  "brawl_fighter": "What's most important when you're a fighter is grit. Brawl Fighter knows all about that, and he'll be the first to tell you: If you're ready to hit, you should be ready to get hit. The spiked knuckles don't have a complaints department to hear your issues.", // Brawl Fighter
  "cutthroat_assassin": "A person like this has no sensitivity for violence, having performed routine and cold-blooded murder so many times that he has a chillingly nonspecific euphemism for it. Approach a man like this with the utmost of caution if you need a job done. Better yet, send a letter and don't approach him at all.", // Cutthroat Assassin
  "poisonblade_assassin": "A vial of the harshest gear to be found this side of the endless mountains is enough to turn one garden-breed psychopath into a problem for nearly anyone else. He likes when his victims die more slowly because he savours the satisfaction. What a creep.", // Poisonblade Assassin
  "blood_sage": "Some people have perverse appetites, and the Blood Sage is one whose particular brand is not usually of harm to anyone else. Somewhere obscure and in the wild, he pricks himself with a pin, divining fortunes from the gentle trickle down his finger. However, exiled and infringed upon by others, this sage has developed a painful ritual of revenge.", // Blood Sage
  "fateweaver_sage": "This sage can interact with the flow of time and fabric of space, each in small measure. By warping these around himself, he can create effects that even mages struggle to understand. What's really funny is that using Realm Warp to get around doesn't even cost him any extra AP compared to walking, so he likes to freak people out by doing that sometimes.", // Fateweaver Sage
  "swashbuckle_plunderer": "This plunderer will never stop telling you of his extraordinary deeds. Been somewhere? He's been somewhere farther, and there were also probably also dragons there, not to mention plenty of air guitar. You never want to have to share a dinner table with this guy, by golly.", // Swashbuckle Plunderer
  "twinaxe_plunderer": "Since the dawn of agriculture, the plunderers who were most successful in raiding others' crop stores were those whose farming gave them deadly strength and skill with their implements. This raider has shortened the handles of the axes he used to clear his land, ready to reap the spoils of another with one in each hand.", // Twinaxe Plunderer
  "daring_cavalier": "Lead a horse to water, it won't necessarily drink. Lead a man to a horse, on the other hand, and give it water? Oh jeez. Can I start over? Okay, lead the water to a horseman and- damn it. Okay. This horseman is a knight, he and the horse both drink water, and it takes a lot to provide for a horse out here in addition to yourself so you know he must be an important knight to ride in on one.", // Daring Cavalier
  "orders_chosen": "This knight was chosen by the Order of the Open Book to wield the magical set of artifacts passed down through their order now, in their time of need. They march against the Faceless King, leaving no blessing or boon off the table from their years as collectors of ancient lore.", // Order's Chosen
  "ironclad_peacekeeper": "This old knight has seen battle more times than most people could believe, and survived every one while standing between his allies and the enemy. His skill and perserverance earn him huge respect on the battlefield, as does his beaten-in steel shield, tempered harder by battle than the forge that fired it.", // Hardened Peacekeeper
  "vanguard_commander": "The Vanguard Commander is a type of unit deployed at intervals as much for a morale boost as for protection, since seeing them fighting along an orderly line informs others where the battle lines are drawn and pushes their efforts forward as their banner yet waves from the back of the Vanguard's customized armour.", // Vanguard Commander
  "nexus_sorcerer": "This sorcerer, inspired by tales of lifetimes-long crossings between this realm and the one beyond the mountains, quickly set to work developing a spell that could translocate two different beings. When she finally arrives on the other side of her long voyage, she already has a whole list of people she has already agreed to help portal accross, for a small fee.", // Nexus Sorcerer
  "catalyst_curator": "The curator of catalysts seeks the purest crystals in large quantities, always experimenting with magical conductivity and pushing them to their limits. She has no patience for those who treasure their gemstones as valuables. She insists that spending gems in pursuit of the progress of magic is necessary, since aside from conducting magic, the stones have no other useful properties.", // Catalyst Curator
  "leyline_invoker": "The leyline invoker sees the flow of magic, and the journey AP takes from a unit past the hidden veil of the arcane immaterial. This does not give the invoker full control over magic's flow, but she can nonetheless cause the veil to be torn open in select areas, spilling a hazardous flow of magic temporarily from the tear until the magical weave rematerializes to contain it.", // Leyline Invoker
  "frostbinder": "The frostbinder is an often misunderstood wizard that is difficult to explain briefly. What manifests as simple ice magic is really a control over heat more generally, and her powers can cause even the molecules in a living being to slow down or speed up. The nuance and technicality of such spells is not entirely lost on the battlefield, where enemies' movements seem to visibly slow around her.", // Frostbinder
  "barbarian_tyrant": "There are those among the realms of man for whom the great period of civil war was not a misfortune, but an opportunity to claim through might anything the chaos might place within their grasps. The Barbarian Tyrant is one such scoundrel, whose technique with a crushing blade and handaxe have earned him piles of riches and followers, outside of both the king's law and the disciplined order of any rebel group.", // Barbarian Tyrant
  "veteran_armsmaster": "This master of the blade developed a flowing technique with a strange blade forged in an obscure and faraway land. Nobody else can perfectly mirror him with the weapon, try as many successfully have to replicate the rigourous techinique with which the sword was forged. In his advanced years, this master has opened a school where pupils learn the correct form with which to wield them.", // Veteran Armsmaster
  "defiant_adept": "An adept is one in whom the flow of magic awakened on its own, without needing to be forced through training. This young prodigy has been incorigible ever since his powers awakened as an adept, insisting on goofing off and shirking practice tips from others in favour of his own techniques. After all, who else can wield a floating weapon like he can, and at such a young age?", // Defiant Adept
  "skirmish_captain": "This captain was inspired by an old oral legend of a hero fighting with only his nation's flag fastened to a long pole. Though not exactly the case for him, he was inspired to fight using a similar technique under a broader red flag, representing the liberation of all humanity from the rule of the Faceless King.", // Skirmish Captain
  "wielder_of_night": "This assassin has perfected a technique for the manipulation of shadow, allowing them to hide in plain sight. By using this technique to shroud themself and wait for the perfect time to strike, they can achieve more through simple fundamentals than almost any other assassin.", // Wielder of Night
  "blight_phantom": "While many have communed with supernatural forces in the realms of man, few have communed directly with the spirits of the afterlife. When the troubled and sick mind of an assassin was brought into communion with the spirits of vengeful killers long since passed away, a strange accord between living and dead was made that more of the deserving might join the ranks of the ghosts by the Blight Phantom's blade.", // Blight Phantom
  "high_seas_captain": "It is said that women are bad luck at sea. She has long protested this, and even joked that it results from the burning desire of men to play around with each other privately aboard their boats. But what she doesn't realize is that, with each pirate ship she sinks, her pony-tailed sillhouette peering at escapee rowboats through a spyglass as many are blown away with cannons only lends credence to the old saying.", // High Seas Captain
  "corsair_saboteur": "This pirate believes that nothing great accomplished at sea truly survives to be told of on land unless it is done with a certain flaire and panache. He stages the explosions of enemy vessels as a spectacle, swinging back to his own ship with the last of the booty using his grappling hook only once carefully timed fuses are lit and the feather in his hat is properly straightened.", // Corsair Saboteur
  "grandfather_mystic": "The Grandfather Mystic sees the truth of the land beyond the endless mountains, teeming with magic and opportunity, should one young enough resolve to make the crossing and grasp at it. He tells the truth in his stories, but only those with warrior's intuition know him as other than a madman. The proof is in his meditation. The man has been seen levitating inches above the ground, as his insightful predictions magically lighten the spirit.", // Grandfather Oracle
  "frenzied_burster": "The reveal that the Faceless King was not human came with more consequences than everyone know about. Secretly, he subsumed certain key subjects in his court over the years, gaining for himself their intellect and leaving their empty shells to live on as extensions of his own eyes and ears. One such spy, found out among his peers, bursts forth now from this unit, instintually counting on its shapeshifter strength to win the day.", // Frenzied Burster
  "giant_boar": "While many humans keep swine as livestock, no one has ever successfully tamed a boar of this size. They are fiercely territorial, charging their prey on sight and goring them deep with their long tusks. The largest of these creatures have been said to fight each other in large piles over prey that is difficult to dislodge from another's tusks, the original hunter often securing precious little of its own prey.", // Giant Boar
  "siege_mammoth": "It did not take long for the potential of this creature to be realized in combat after the period of civil war began. With their giant stature, carrying capacity, and resistance, the mammoth pacyderms of the frozen provinces frequently had their fur trimmed to suit the temperature of other locales. They carried infantry and all manner of heavy armaments, and provided immeasureable frontline pressure in their own right.", // Siege Mammoth
  "savage_grizzly": "The only regular animal with the raw, primal power to challenge any other on land, even those that are supernatural. Summoners have boasted of clearing a dozen men from a fortified position by spending only a single spell to call one forth.", // Savage Grizzly
  "spitfire_drake": "A classic, firebreathing example of a drake, the beastly airbourne terrors whose progeny outnumber all others in the savage skies above the endless mountains. These creatures resemble lizards of the land, but they fly with webbed wings and emit chemicals from a gland above their tongue which combust or otherwise react with the outside air. Though not true dragons, that fact does nothing to contest the drakes' undeniable rulership of the skies.", // Spitfire Drake
  "tempest_roc": "This mythical bird is a roc in the form of an all-white bird. As rocs can command the winds of the building storm that blocks passage through the higher parts of the endless mountains, they are the only aerial creature to openly fly the most hazardous skies that are otherwise the sole domain of elder drakes, greater direwyrms, and true dragons.", // Tempest Roc
  "corrosive_wyvern": "A wyvern is a hybridized creature born from the union of a giant serpent with a drake, a combination frequently misattributed to direwyrms. This particular one wields a sizzling venom powerful enough to melt through humans' armour like butter. In the skies it patrols, a creature without such an advantage might be consumed by larger, thick-scaled elder drakes.", // Corrosive Wyvern
  "carapace_crusher": "There are those wise sages who say that while all humans are in some form kin to one another, the same cannot be said of crabs. This giant example, they claim, diverged from a line entirely its own, as did the myriad other beings that through the passage of time have manifested in similar orderly, chitinous shapes. Destiny seems to dictate that such will always be the shape of the shoreline's true inheritors.", // Carapace Crusher
  "octopod_titan": "While the pressure underwater keeps it contained, the surface bloats the otherwise lithe form of the typical octopus. This example has adapted thicker skin to become a force of nature on land, though nevertheless it thrashes and makes no hesistation angrily punishing those who drew it out of its comforting waters.", // Octopod Titan
  "marsh_hydra": "This multi-headed beast of legend hails from the other side of the endless mountains, a long and arduous journey from which almost no humans have ever returned. Nonetheless, the old mage who witnessed the hydra with his own eyes trusted his people to recognise and wield its regenerative secrets to cure disease, sending it countless miles home with the last of his summoning magic. The species now terrorizes the southwestern edge of a province along the endless mountains, having slain countless warriors sent there to slay them.", // Marsh Hydra
  "gateway_guardians": "These knights were awarded the honour of guarding the most assailled door in the realms of man, the gate to the Faceless King's castle. There is honour still in defending the capital of the realm's golden age and the monarch whose rule brought it forth, even as many in the realms of man see their ruler as a deceptive freak of nature.", // Gateway Guardians
  "drakerider_paladin": "This paladin conquerered the oppressive heights of one of the nearest of the endless mountains. The staggering feat brought him to tempest altitudes and into contact with many drakes, one of whom he was forced to befriend through combat to survive the ordeal. In the end, he flew down with the mark of a mission accomplished and a majestic mount nearly mistakable for that of an avatar.", // Drakerider Paladin
  "animus_twin": "These two bicker ALL the time about who gets to wear the hat. They're equally powerful, and both of them are still mentally in there, but they share a body because their soul-fusion ritual ran out of magic power partway. Still, many make the mistake of underestimating just how deadly the pair can be in combat.", // Animus Twin
  "starburst_wizard": "This mage of legend wields power over the very stars. It is unclear how he communes with such a distant force, being more remote even than the sun and the moon. What most do not know about the Starburst Wizard is the sheer amount of magical attunement that went into his creation, including but not limited to a fusion between 2 archmages thought long-dead.", // Starburst Wizard
  "dawnglow_archer": "In a move which inspired more than one questionable theatrical rendition, a pair of fighters left with nothing but a bow without arrows against a group of charging knights came up with a plan. Some magics are known even to common people, and this team knew a peculiar scroll to turn one man into ammunition for the other to fire. For his fearlessness in performing the spell, he instead became an endless quiver of light for his companion.", // Dawnglow Archer
  "breaker_swordsman": "In a plot to create the most powerful swordsman known to man, the Faceless King himself once ordered two blades forged in secret, each containing a gem imbued with a fusion spell. Then, after holding the ultimate tournament for all the realm's fighters, the two finalists were given the blades. What happened when they clashed is self-explanatory. He now leads a group of rebels against the one who fused him.", // Breaker Swordsman
  "blade_singer": "Though bald on top, this swordsman has 100% coverage in battle by virtue of the ring of swords he keeps constantly spinning around him. He has a gift to sing in such a tone that blades enchanted with a magical purpose will often obey the call and fall among his floating weapons. Perhaps many do so out of respect for the deadly and efficient artistry he finds in his craft, even as he lives a harsh life consumed by battle.", // Blade Singer
  "gemstone_paladin": "This paladin, after hearing the story of the Amethyst Mage, made it his mission to use the gemstones found in the deep caverns to be a protector and an inspiration to those who toil under exploitation in the various mines found there. By showing labourers the power of gems, he aims to liberate indentured workers in every mine he can find, one by one.", // Gemstone Paladin
  "hexbinder": "Originally a ruin explorer, the Hexbinder fell victim time again to those deadly magics used to defend tombs and ancient strongholds where magical knowledge is often lost. In exploring these ruins and tenaciously persisting, the Hexbinder developed an advanced repertoire of tricks to disarm magic that make him a popular hire in other areas now, including as a mercenary.", // Hexbinder
  "lobber_gang": "They wheel along with them a catapult meant for large ammunition that they cannot bring along, try as they might with carts and beasts of burden. Their solution? Use the foe as ammunition, employing any trickery necessary to seat or stand them on the end of the arm as the lever is pulled.", // Lobber Gang
  "blind_seer": "When an ancient sage and a fighter had a fateful meeting, they spoke all day, finally reflecting to each other at the end that they would trade lives given the chance. A brooch whose power was unknown to the fighter then radiated from his pocket, fusing the life forces of the 2 so the old sage's wisdom might then pervade the open battlefield once more.", // Blind Seer
  "shadowguard": "This knight was the automaton of a great evil lord, made only of shadow and commanded by his will alone to defend his citadel. Or so it was until the armour was claimed by a great hero, defeating the spirit inside with a powerful artifact. Now, the one who wears it wields shadow neither for good nor for evil.", // Shadowguard
  "dreadnought_privateer": "Nobody else alive is known to have sunk as many ships as the Dreadnought Privateer, and the proof is in his vessel. His own ship is a jumbled mish-mash of all the most seaworth components found on hundreds of other vessels, whose remains besides these are nowhere else to be found, sunken at the bottom of the sea.", // Dreadnought Privateer
  "magnetic_marauder": "Not content risking his own hull for a plunder, the Magnetic Marauder takes advantage of a strange device found among his more typical loot years ago. Finding that it drew metals at a short distance, he fiddled with it until, using magic, the streams of attraction and repulsion coming from within could be more tightly controlled.", // Magnetic Marauder
  "harsh_inquisitor": "Once, a remote kingdom made a violent pact to expunge magic, in all its forms, throughout the world. Clearly insurmountable though this task was, the initiative nontheless resulted in some top-of-the-line combatants filled to the brim with hatred and the magical power to back it up. A Harsh Inquisitor is one such warrior, bringing runic steel to bear against all who speak their hexes in vain.", // Harsh Inquisitor
  "heavy_cannoneer": "This pirate wields the strength of many lesser men to carry a small cannon around as personal firepower. Accompanied by her blazing cannons, the Heavy Cannoneer provides artillery support better than any other individual, loading the armaments with supernatural ease.", // Heavy Cannoneer
  "prismatic_pikemen": "These pikemen found a bright and colourful geyser of liquid one day coming out of the earth in a remote battlefield, far in the endless mountains and at untold height. As a savage drakeling swooped in from above, the pair had no choice but to dive into the pool the geyser left behind. The entity of this pond accepted their bravery, and granted them its power.", // Prismatic Pikemen
  "codex_defender": "Don't ask what chivalric order this guy comes from. Just don't. Not because he won't tell you, of course. Just that I forgot what the answer was already since he actually does not stop talking. You will have told him 'that's crazy' easily 5 times and this guy will no joke be finding you a quotation from the big scroll.", // Codex Defender
  "sparring_partners": "Every night, after the sun had set and the moon illuminated the clearing between their two camps, the two met in secret. They fought wordlessly, but no longer as enemies. Their bond was one that only two true warriors can share, and one day it inspired the two armies to unite against a common enemy. Such is the founding legend of a stronghold town in the mountains that has sworn off war.", // Sparring Partners
  "elite_sniper": "As a fighter was beset by an assassin on uneven terrain well into a battle, they had a mortal clash, their steel ringing so violently that both weapons slipped from their owners' hands. Both determined not to let the other get he upper hand, a discarded alien weapon nearby caught their eye at the same time. Now, they wield it together as one of the only fusion-people known to have resulted from outside experimentation.", // Elite Sniper
  "warden_of_the_gate": "The composition and alignment of the materials in his armour prevent summoning magic from being used in his vicinity. This experienced knight remembers a day when there were many more of his kind, sent in against demonic invasions to stop the flow of invaders coming through their hellish portals.", // Warden of the Gate
  "simian_sovereign": "He's the ruler of the monkey gang, you're doubtless familiar. He's come back again, and now he just might kill ya. He's larger than before, and his speed has increased. He throw the largest of bananas with the greatest of ease. So don't look at this ape like you've seen him before. The monkies' fearless leader? Now he's ready for war!", // Simian Sovereign
  "cannon_squadron": "What's stronger than 3 knights on a mission to ransack rebel hamlets? When one hamlet in particular gave this group deadly trouble, they asked themselves this question in just the right company. With weaponry borrowed from a naval ship, they've now come back with their idea of a siege engine designed to take the place by force.", // Cannon Squadron
  "anima_magi": "The Anima Magi are a council of 3 mages sharing one fused, incredibly powerful soul. Using their powers combined, they tapped into the primal flow of magic and harnessed a portion of the ineffable stream for themselves. At any given point these guys probably have more than 4AP stored up, we just make them play by the rules so that it doesn't rain arcane lightning everywhere.", // Anima Magi
  "renegade_trio": "These three renegades cannot afford to get caught. They are wanted, at loose, and on the run from the law. At the same time, they are at the height of their success. These guys have never seen such a fat pile of cash roll in as they're getting now from their string of robberies. Village to village, they take all they can and move on to the next. A larger group of bandits would have already gotten caught.", // Renegade Trio
  "faceless_king": "The event that first launched the realms of men into a cycle of civil war was the revelation that their lawful monarch was secretly a shapeshifter. Though he knew well enough to hide it, he never really understood why this was a bad thing. The humans had kept their monarchy so insular that none of them even noticed when a more advanced and capable being joined their ranks, attempting to make a change. Why, he asks, do they reject him for who he is, when the height of his rule was considered their Golden Age?", // Faceless King
  "the_cyclotron": "An advanced machine that targets degenerate gamblers and consumes them to synthesize new fuel, people never even knew something like the Cyclotron was possible. All signs pointed to no. But from deep in a disgustingly overfunded royal lab somewhere, this fancifully decorated automaton managed to escape, luring others to its remote lair who truly seek a test of their good fortune.", // The Cyclotron

  // ---- Wrath of the Elements ----
  "frozen_knight": "Left to his post to fend for himself, this forgotten knight never gave up even as a ruthless and seemingly neverending winter came and swallowed the outpost he defended. Now, as though by the same magic that quietly took the outpost from him, he takes his sustinence from the cold and drives his lance deep into any who yet threaten his post.", // Frozen Knight
  "frozen_fighter": "This fighter breathes thick into cool mountain air each morning as he wakes with the sun and trains with his mace, refusing to yield to harsh weather or to any opposing raiders. After a spending his childhood on a farm that had struck a deal with local pirates for survival, he swore that when he started his own farm one day, it would never fall victim to anyone in the same way.", // Frozen Fighter
  "frozen_lancer": "This lancer has learned to perfect a technique for sliding on ice, and uses it to glide around the battlefield with an ease others struggle to match. His momentum drives forth a lance fashioned after an icicle, which steals the warmth from the pierced hearts of his slain foes via a simple enchantment. This brutal technique has seen him through several battles in the harsh mountain terrain.", // Frozen Lancer
  "frozen_golem": "When the carrot was placed on the snow-person's nose, it rose to life to defend a group of mischeivous children playing in the mountains from an enraged abominable snowman. It is unclear what happened to the original snow defender, but golems in the same fashion have since frequently been created in snowy regions as defenders, after the childrens' story was cleverly adapted into an entry in a popular spellbook.", // Frozen Golem
  "frozen_wildcat": "This cat's thick fur lets very little cold escape, the the thickness of it doubles as an absorber of harsh impacts and otherwise lethal slashes. The fierce arboreal predator pounces forth with razor-like claws and teeth like stilettos, knowing each scrap of meat she brings home to her cubs may make the difference between life and death in the harsh tundra.", // Frozen Wildcat
  "flaming_fighter": "What makes a fighter a fighter is ultimately their resolve, not their weapon. This particular one was tasked with lighting the beacons to warn neighbouring armies of the incoming enemy forces. He goes to complete his mission even now as his armaments are lost, fighting instead with two lit torches and a flaming ferocity.", // Flaming Fighter
  "flaming_mage": "He once fell in love with a girl named Ruby. Haha, sike! Could you imagine it was some corny thing like that? He likes fire, bro. He likes the colour red. He shoots Ruby Ray because he needed a ruby in order to focus the fire magic enough for a long-range shot.", // Flaming Mage
  "flaming_salamander": "The fearsome salamander, a relative of the ancient serpent, has four dextrous limbs and elementally attunes only with fire. They must live where there is sweltering heat, the damage from which they resist entirely, to fuel their cold-blooded physiologies. They are even known to consume molten lava and spit it at their enemies.", // Flaming Salamander
  "flaming_drakeling": "Even the young of the fire drake, the most commonly known type of drake to humans, can be deadly in its own right. Some summoners, enamoured with the properties of such fierce summons, waste no extra energy calling forth an adult one. The ritual to bring forth the chick of the drake species costs far less AP to perform, and leaves most enemies no less burnt in its wake.", // Flaming Drakeling
  "flaming_ooze": "While it might be mistaken for a pile of lava, the flaming ooze is a proper ooze that has subsumed the element of fire. The more heat it consumes, the more powerful and large it becomes, and sometimes when it is at capacity the only way for such an ooze to process heat it can no longer digest is to radiate it from the countless microscopic pores along its body. Standing nearby can be sweltering if not lethal.", // Flaming Ooze
  "plant_mage": "This mage lives in the southern jungle, just outside the reaches of any human country. She survives among the wildlife by chanelling natural energies through her jade crystal, allowing her to manipulate plants' physical bodies as well as emulate their natural defense mechanisms.", // Plant Mage
  "plant_knight": "The green thing on this knight's helmet is her hair. She dyed it green, and getting it to look good was difficult compared to other colours she's tried. Her knightly inspiration came from a story of a knight aligned with plants, so she grew her axe from a single piece of enchanted green hardwood in honour of the legendary character. Green Execution can be a funny party trick when a good enough healer is present.", // Plant Knight
  "plant_lasher": "Not every plant can move. In fact, most can't. The Plant Lasher's motivation for uprooting is pure revenge. This hateful creature can be flattened and shredded and still grow back, hiding against the grass and waiting to lash hatefully at the ankles of unsuspecting humans passing by. After all, how dare we misuse the earth, our mother, so audaciously when her servants yet grow on her surface to defend her?", // Plant Lasher
  "noxious_plant": "This plant, highly sought after by alchemists, has developed a taste for human armour, not our flesh. Using the harshest and most toxic digestive compounds, this plant can break down tempered metal armours into robust nutrition for itself, of which it requires plenty to synthesize new acids and continue on its simple life cycle.", // Noxious Plant
  "jaw_plant": "This plant has a mouth to chew and swallow live prey with, and it digests us for energy so it can roam forth to defend the forested realms from further exploitation at the hands of humans. These plants were grown in the deepest of forests for just such a purpose en-masse, since generally bringing the fight to others is not the plant kingdom's strong suit.", // Jaw Plant
  "abominable_snowman": "This creature of myth prowls the frozen mountaintops under the cover of blizzards, but mostly keeps to its cave when it is not out hunting large game. The fur all around the ape-like creature's body renders it almost completely impervious to cold, and its terrifying near-supernatural strength and stature lead many to assume that is not a beast that evolved of its own accord.", // Abominable Snowman
  "frostbreath_howler": "This supernatural beast wields the power of windchill, stripping the skin from its prey's bones before devouring it whole with its giant, gaping mouth. There is a popular myth about this creature stemming from the shape of its horns, that a screaming, greedy billy goat took this form when met with the chaotic magical energies roiling atop a high peak in the endless mountains. It is believeable, strong climbers such as goats are.", // Frostbreath Howler
  "burning_rager": "I would be precisely as mad as this guy too, if someone set me on fire. That's not why he rages though. This screaming creature is crossed between a human and a fire elemental as a result of a strange ritual. Regardless of how it formed, the Burning Rager and its kin are set loose on battlefields to spread wildfire, specializing in crowd control. Little is known of their personal habits.", // Burning Rager
  "lava_elemental": "The forces of the earth waged an endless battle against each other, content forever to strengthen and hold each other in balance. As humans now go to war, the rage of the earth continued to build as their trespasses against the land grew and compounded to fuel building war efforts. That very rage, and the intent behind it, boil now within the Lava Elemental, whose scorching heat radiates hotter than fire.", // Lava Elemental
  "hungering_overgrowth": "The Hungering Overgrowth was a herbivorous plant that devoured only other plants, strangling and consuming their roots to strengthen itself. Though reviled among plants, their differences are easily set aside as things are taken less personally in the plant kingdom. The overgrowth finds its place now on the battlefield, and its newfound taste for human flesh has become no less ravenous than its hunger for its own kind.", // Hungering Overgrowth
  "seed_bombardier": "Plants can spread in various ways depending the type. Some have seeds, others have spores. The Seed Bombardier has both, and its seeds emit its spores. If either component takes root, it grows the other as a matter of course. This ingeniously adapted plant has therefore spent all of its evolutionary and adaptational power since gaining this feature on molding itself to launch its projectiles as far as possible.", // Seed Bombardier
  "voracious_firemaw": "The Voracious Firemaw, though resembling a dragon, is an earthbound species of giant lizard hailing from the deep desert wastes. Its flaming breath exploits its dried out prey as it pops out from beneath the desert sands and easily sets them on fire. The firemaw has no concept of a medium-rare. Its meat is always cooked to a sizzlingly hot char.", // Voracious Firemaw
  "bonechiller_greatwurm": "The friction created by these long, supernaturally enlarged creatures as they tunnel through the earth generates a large amount of heat, precluding them from living in too hot of a locale. As an adaptation, the normally arctic-dwelling greatwurms have sometimes been given frost enchantments by human enchanters hoping to exploit them as weapons, or are fed a diet high in euclase for its cold-aligned properties.", // Bonechiller Greatwurm
  "lumbering_treeback": "This ancient turtle has lived long enough for other forms of life to live and die on top of its shell. Most recently, an entire tree has sprouted, taking root in the crevices and feeding off the nutrients therein. This symbiotic creature of great patience shows incredible intelligence for a reptile, not to mention an uncommon compassion to those who it does not decide to snap immediately into its vice-like jaws.", // Lumbering Treeback
  "canyonguard_iceberg": "When the humans of the realms of man decided to exploit the earth beyond its capacity for self-repair, the endless struggle between natural forces quietly came to a halt. The canyonguards are some of the most imposing frontline battering rams of the elemental armies, clearing the way for fiery, icy, and plant forces alike to march against the lines of humans broken by their brutal, icy clubs.", // Canyonguard Iceberg
  "volcanic_tyrant": "When the elemental forces first arranged that an accord was to be negotiated in order to fight the humans, they met on a neutral plateau between the hot jungle and the frozen tundra. There, a volcano sprouted, and the leader of the fiery armies took a draconic form, bursting from beneath the earth to fiercely negotiate his terms with the elder treants and ancient ice elementals. Today, that spot is the heart of the firelands.", // Volcanic Tyrant
  "elder_pine_treant": "Plants don't see hierarchy or adversity like humans do, viewing each other roughly as equals. That said, the most ancient among them silently command respect, and none moreso than the treants, greatest among plants in stature and range of influence. The pine treants in particular share their sap with travellers of the north who are lucky enough to find them. Or, that was the case until the war against humans began.", // Elder Pine Treant
  "direfrost_spectre": "The direfrost spectre is another assassin who, like some others, made a pact with another in the afterlife to send them souls. In this case, the wraith holds the power of hoarfrost, and the pact was made out of a cold desperation.", // Direfrost Spectre
  "firebrand_raider": "The spectacle of fire reflected on water set against an evening sunset: The Firebrand Raider considers himself an artist. Some fail to realize amidst his chaos that he is a fusion person formed of a sly pyromaniac and a poetic pirate.", // Firebrand Raider
  "spore_mystic": "This mystic has allowed fungus to engulf him, growing a mushroom cap over his head and allowing its spores to permeate his body. His power allows him to rapidly sprout mushrooms bearing his magic almost anywhere he chooses.", // Spore Mystic

  // ---- Fury of the Skies ----
  "nimbus_mage": "This mage commands the power the wind and clouds, and uses it to subtly aid his allies and cut through his foes armour. The air permeates all on the battlefield, and though it mostly goes unseen, all will feel the harsh bite of his weapon of choice.", // Nimbus Mage
  "nimbus_assassin": "For this assassin, the clouds are heavy enough to step on, and he bounds accross the air to his target with an alarming speed. Many have no opportunity to adapt to such a fighting style before he pulls the air silently from their lungs with his cloud-shaped dagger.", // Nimbus Assassin
  "nimbus_drakeling": "This white drakeling is the young of a solitary species residing outside the great tempest in calmer skies. They are considered good fortune in those remote parts of the world where airships are flown. Nonetheless, no worse fate could befall a flock of migratory birds than to meet one.", // Nimbus Drakeling
  "frozen_nimbus": "This nimbus is a cloud containing an elemental spirit of ice, granting it power windchill like the limb of a greater force of nature. It can be a major nuissance to forces progressing through cold terrain.", // Frozen Nimbus
  "flaming_nimbus": "A Flaming Nimbus might be formed when geothermal gasses trapped beneath the earth meet with the stray magical influence of summoners. They command heat, manifesting as rolling balls of scalding steam that set the ground alight beneath them as they float along in the breeze.", // Flaming Nimbus
  "lightning_nimbus": "The weakest yet most common type of creature in the great tempest is the Lightning Nimbus, an electricity-imbued cloud that continually seeks more and more static friction. It charges up as much as it can before releasing crackling lightning all around its body.", // Lightning Nimbus
  "lightning_fighter": "The Battle Engineer never should have given this guy a battery. Just look at him. He thinks his lightning sword is going to accomplish something on the battlefield. He's right of course. And he's quite clever, as many opponents' blades should readily conduct electricity. Still, you'd think more people would be doing stuff like this if it were actually a good idea as a whole.", // Lightning Fighter
  "lightning_plant": "This plant soaks in the energies of the earth through its roots, manifesting as electricity that eminates from its lightning-shaped fruit. It can be eaten once picked, and is said to be quite delicious. However, the plant welcomes any human to try to pick it.", // Lightning Plant
  "lightning_assassin": "This killer wields magical daggers imbued with power taken from the eternal tempest. When he channels their power into his body, he can move at supernatural speeds and fry opponents with electrical slashes and stabs.", // Lightning Assassin
  "lightning_wildcat": "This cat can move with the speed of lightning when it charges enough electricity into its fur from moving around or stealing it from opponents with its claws. The fur's texture changes from wild and frizzy to neat and straight after a sudden discharge.", // Lightning Wildcat
  "lightning_ooze": "This ooze, rather than being made of a good electrical conductor, is made of a material that is almost a complete insulator, letting no electrical movement through. Static between two materials can therefore build to hazardous levels within this creature before it releases any from its body.", // Lightning Ooze
  "lunar_assassin": "Many assassins move only at night, relying on the light of the moon. But to be truly lunar, one must resolve solemnly to complete a mission of greater purpose beneath this light. This assassin's purpose is to slay the unworthy rebels who sully the Faceless King's great age with war.", // Lunar Assassin
  "lunar_lancer": "This lancer is one of few warriors who, under moonlight, swore a solemn oath of the heart to accomplish a task no matter the cost. This made him lunar, and enshrined in his lance of shining silver the blessings of patience and serenity, allowing it to pierce impure and the unworthy souls who oppress the weak.", // Lunar Lancer
  "lunar_wildcat": "When the night-adder accepted a mount in its home glade and gave the moon an avatar without being summoned, the primordial lunar spirit spread its tendrils wide. For it had not answered the avatar ritual, and could not be embarassed among its peers to lack a beastly champion were someone to perform it thenceforth. This cat of pure black, humble as it is, somehow gained the moon's blessing this way.", // Lunar Wildcat
  "solar_knight": "This knight, though average in skill, represents the blazing impetus of the sun in his shining armour and boldness in battle. The harsh light demands immediacy and decisive action, so he charges headlong with faith in his solar blessings to win him the day.", // Solar Knight
  "solar_drakeling": "This drakeling's gleaming scales reflect the sun's light in all different colours and directions, making it one of the most heavily distracting foes to fight on the battlefield and one of the hardest to land a direct hit on with a ranged attack. It hides inside the clouds before ambushing prey above in sunlight.", // Solar Drakeling
  "solar_lancer": "To be solar is to keep moving forward with unfaltering consistency. The solar lancer sees this as intertwined with the ideals of lancing, and drives a point with a curved edge to more easily slice through his prey in motion. Its shape resembles a flaming arm of the golden sun.", // Solar Lancer
  "toxic_ooze": "This toxic ooze has digestive enzymes permeating each section of its body, powerful enough to dissolve steel the same way a human might digest an afternoon biscuit. It splashes carelessly, spreading these fluids everywhere and sopping up any screaming victims that sizzle at their touch.", // Toxic Ooze
  "storm_rogue": "The quickest rogues are the greatest, or so says the Storm Rogue. To take honing his reflexes to the most extreme heights, he literally upped his altitude and took on the multitude wildlife of the endless mountains. When he reached the summit of a large range in the extreme west, his training had finally become complete.", // Storm Rogue
  "overcharged_rootnexus": "Though most plants rely on natural forces to grow, there are many that tap into magic to grow in strange ways. The Overcharged Rootnexus is one that does so indiscriminately, soaking magic through its roots in any form it can grab hold of. In turn, these roots are strengthened and move at incredible speeds through the soil.", // Overcharged Rootnexus
  "fulgur_scale_skywyrm": "The complex ancestries of the various flying reptiles of this world get no simpler factoring in Skywyrms, the progeny of direwyrms and drakes. Is it our misfortune that such varied and fearsome lizards roam our skies, or a great stroke of luck that the territorial creatures mostly keep to fighting each other for supremacy?", // Fulgur-Scale Skywyrm
  "firebrand_wingserpent": "Not limited to humans, the process of fusion can combine any two beings that share a purpose, willing or not. Therefore, long ago, the practice of hybridizing familiars became commonplace among learned wizards looking to flex their mettle to their peers.", // Firebrand Wingserpent
  "zenith_charger": "This impatient lancer paid handsomely to have an enchantment placed on her armour granting her supernatural speed. Talentless as a rider, she nonetheless drives her lances home through their target, on foot, running faster along the ground at her own pace than any steed could carry her.", // Zenith Charger
  "boastful_champion": "This champion, past his prime, was once an unstoppable force in the arena. Charging forth atop a handsome thoroughbred stallion bought with his prize money, and clad in shining armour, the Boastful Champion keeps an old habit in hanging a piece of metal scrap around his neck to memorialize each victory.", // Boastful Champion
  "eclipse_prowler": "As time passed and the varied moonblessed beasts of the night grew, their primordial spirit willed it that only the strong may survive to be called upon as beasts of the avatar ritual. Prowling the night uncontested to this day is one mountain lion, who was acknowledged as leader of her pride beneath the ceremony of a solar eclipse.", // Eclipse Prowler
  "jungle_stalker": "One of the creatures most feared in the jungle at the southern border of humanity's realms is presumed to take the shape of a giant, killer feline due to the marks it leaves on its prey. This terrifying Jungle Stalker will sometimes leave brutalized prey just to mark its territority, showing horrifying gruesomeness and destructive power.", // Jungle Stalker
  "caustic_terror_slime": "More powerful than an ordinary slime the terror-slime terrorizes its prey by possessing more flexible and adaptable physical attributes than other slimes, seeming at once to be able to contain any number of surfaces on its body with various different properties. These can be traits like bouncy, sticky, corrosive, squishy, or quick-moving in the case of limblike tendrils.", // Caustic Terror-Slime
  "great_gel_prism": "This giant cube of gel can compress and expand the dimensions of its body to fit through different spaces, but always remains roughly in the shape of a rectangular prism as though its corners won't bend. It ruthlessly subsumes any life form it rolls across, dissolving it slowly as it is forced to sit motionless and suffocate.", // Great Gel Prism
  "feverish_manifestation": "Stare into the fire long enough, the the fire starts to stare back. Literally, in this case. The swirling eyes and wide grin of the face in the fire commands pyromania into the heart of careless observers.", // Feverish Manifestation
  "glacial_monolith": "Akin to the canyonguards, a Glacial Monolith is an ice elemental animated by powerful magic. These are the work of living summoners who commit portions of their magical power persistently to channel the spell. Its arcane powers are thus amplified beyond what a regular ice elemental can manage.", // Glacial Monolith
  "moons_acolyte": "The Moon's Acolyte only strikes on nights of the full moon, and because of his drumming, everyone hears him coming. Its rhythm summons the most unfortunate and forgotten creatures, filling them with glee as they dance to its tune. Any who awaken and try to stop the beat quickly find themselves blasted to pieces on-beat by members of the jubilant procession.", // Moon's Acolyte
  "full_moon_strider": "This huge, rare tripod carries with it an eerie fog that constantly hides it from plain view. It is said to be drawn to dreamers of guilty conscience, waking them to the sight of its single piercing eye before violently flattening them with its obsidian feet. A creature of mystery, little is known aside from its allegiance with the moon.", // Full-Moon Strider
  "brightwing_phoenix": "This blazing firebird of legend aligns with the sun, and is said to burn itself out in a nova of flame during its hour of need, before rising the next morning from its own ashes, born again. They are found in all bright colours of the rainbow, each bearing a set of uniquely identifiable feathers, though few have ever been seen.", // Brightwing Phoenix
  "shimmering_bulwark": "She holds a huge, broad shield of brass emblazoned with a pattern resembling the sun's flame. This warrior of the sun stands proudly atop hills and reaches forth with her spear in a prismatic thrust in the image of a solar flare. When fought at night, her shield emits enough magical light to continue her usual tactics for the length of a battle.", // Shimmering Bulwark
  "master_of_weather": "Living alone in a fertile oasis in the very middle of a harsh desert, the Master of Weather is exactly the type of person the trained eye might immediately recognize as fused. Unsubtle in their tactics, they have a penchant for telling their victims the exact method of their demise before taking glee in inflicting it anyway.", // Master of Weather
  "gelatinous_blimp": "This ooze, having subsumed a nimbis spirit, gained the power of flight. It feeds its lighter-than-air gland more and more of its stored nutrients in order to take to the sky, controlling its density by expelling gases, then uses its variable oozelike properties to stick to opponents and smother them.", // Gelatinous Blimp
  "rimewind_direwyrm": "The direwyrm is the most ancient of the flying lizards and one of the most rare, though their unique powers and properties keep them from facing existential threat. Each one commands a force of nature with terrifying potency, and they are among the most powerfully magical beings in existence. This one commands the cold and combines ice powers with its constricting tail and fangs.", // Rimewind Direwyrm
  "biogenic_mass": "Oozes are easily some of the most durable and adaptable life forms, and this one was determined to prove it to a Jaw Plant that ate it without hestitation. Rather than being digested, the stubborn ooze took over the plant's physiological functions from the inside. Now, this uniquely hybridized creature bears the properties of both plant and ooze.", // Biogenic Mass
  "zigzag_cavalry": "This epic cavalier wields two swords that are made of lightning. You read that right. He had a Frostbinder cast a power spell to freeze two bolts of lightning in time, and now he is able to wield them as one would laser swords to deliver devastating jabs and cuts from all angles. He and his horse, longtime partners, charge just like lightning as well.", // Zigzag Cavalry
  "arbiter_of_transience": "It is unclear to most in the Faceless King's court what significance these officials hold. The bald women number only a handful in the realms of man, and their true purpose is as moral guides and interpreters of change for the king, inhuman as he is. His concepts of morality are after all not like ours, and to hide among humans he needed a council of the most learned mages among them to check his decisions before making them.", // Arbiter of Transience
  "rampant_weretiger": "This innocent child was born under the fickle light of the blood moon as his mother suffered the horrible curse of a jungle witch. When the blood moon's light shines on him again, or indeed under the harsh summons of a clever conjurer, he is painfully transformed into the form of a human tiger, clawing for revenge against his helpless wrongdoers one and all.", // Rampant Weretiger
  "tempest_incarnate": "This spirit is allies with the Blustering Gale Spirit. Together, they form the greatest storms known to humanity. This spirit is responsible for the lightning, drawing it indiscriminately through its prey into its charged body.", // Tempest Incarnate
  "blustering_gale_spirit": "This spirit is allies with the Tempest Incarnate. Together, they form the greatest storms known to humanity. This spirit is responsible for the gale force winds, whipping and blasting it in all directions to knock adversaries off their feet and invert them in their flight.", // Blustering Gale Spirit
  "pride_leader_lioness": "The Pride Leader Lioness protects her pack as they roam the savannahs of the southwestern wasteland, teaming up against any large prey that crosses their path. Together, her and a group of weaker lions have even brought down supernatural prey as fearsome as sandsharks.", // Pride Leader Lioness
  "primal_elder_drake": "Drakes have no set lifespan, dying only when they are slain by the other hazardous forces they surround themselves with. This particular one instead shed his wings and contented himself ruling a wide cavern beneath the endless mountains for centuries. Now, as this age of war progresses, the powerful creature awakens from a long slumber to flex its unearthly might and consume everything in its wake.", // Primal Elder Drake
  "sunborn_hierarch": "There have been some tyranical rulers throughout human history branding themselves as sun gods, though few have taken it as literally as the dynasty to which this one belongs. Though very few of his subjects remain, they worship the Sunborn Hierarch as one might the sun itself, believing him its earnest reflection. Though he judges his opposition harshly, for the truly favoured among his followers, the radiant blessings of their king become apparent and manifest.", // Sunborn Hierarch
  "nightruler_cobra": "The Nightruler Cobra is a hypnotizing giant serpent, another of the favoured giant snakes of the moon. The moon's will is fickle and jealous yet patient. In the perfect moment of ambush, the Nightruler will pounce and mesmerize its prey with its bright and smiling face, dancing as it unhinges its jaw for its next unusually willing meal.", // Nightruler Cobra
  "double_dragoon": "Such is the age of war currently befalling the realms of humanity that allegiance no longer wins over strength and a warrior's respect. When the opposing red and blue armies grew tired, insulated from the larger conflict and forgetful of their own objectives, they appointed the strongest lancer on each side to fuse and slay their commanders, marching away from the battlefield together as solemn warriors aligned only to bring about peace and conflict resolution.", // Double Dragoon
  "phalanx_greatooze": "Magical storms, uncommon as they are, can have effects that last long enough to be felt across time. One such storm became the cruel fate of a group of heroic defenders on one island in the eastern archipelago. Though the civilization here is long-gone, the wildlife of the island still has a phalanx-in-one ready to bounce to its aid.", // Phalanx Greatooze
  "radiant_shine_avatar": "This knight rides no less glorious a mount than the golden dragon that embodies the radiant light of the sun, a testiment to the supremacy of his courage among all those nominated by their respective chivalric orders. His role is meant to bring ultimate peace to the realms. The avatar ritual was performed on his behalf by another, as no soul worthy of such power would ever seek it of their own accord. Even now, he rides against the forces of the Faceless King.", // Radiant Shine Avatar
  "serene_glow_avatar": "Since ancient times, the night-adder stalked and ate in its glade beneath the perpetual moonlight in a strange obscure land beyond the endless mountains, her rule contested. That was until a human assassin of incredible patience, having resolved to slay his way through the endless passage to reach beyond the mountains, one day found her. Locked in stalemate, the serpent made the man her avatar, granting him passage home through any shadow cast by the moon's light.", // Serene Glow Avatar

  // ---- Soul Festival 2026 ----
  "skeleton_fighter": "In the bone pits deep beneath the foot of the endless mountains, all metal is melted down in the forges to make more weapons for Skeleton Fighters. The cruel masters who animated them instilled them with the knowledge that defense is secondary, as they can always reassemble from a near-endless supply of bones.", // Skeleton Fighter
  "skeleton_drakeling": "The bones of a drakeling have a unique composition, meaning that these can only be made from genuine drakeling bones. Though much rarer than other types of skeletons, the necromancy used preserves their ability to fly freely and wreck havoc.", // Skeleton Drakeling
  "skeleton_sage": "In the closest facsimile of civilization that skeletons can manage, they always preserve their sages where possible, even those belonging to enemy factions. This is because only those skeletons gifted with necromancy can create more of their kind without living intervention. Otherwise, their bodies would be mere lifeless bone.", // Skeleton Sage
  "calcified_skeleton": "It is long held skeleton lore that the 'undeath' of a living creature is not truly in the flesh or the organs, but in the hair. If it is made of the same material as bone, it stands to reason that their equivalence must be stored there. This skeleton has therefore trained all his undeath for the eventuality of siphoning human vital essence this way.", // Calcified Skeleton
  "skeleton_archer": "Prized highly among skeletons is the mortal art of archery, as allowing the living to close in on them is a surefire way to force oneself to reassemble early and often. This particular one has mastered a technique for hitting a whole group of enemies with arrows all at once.", // Skeleton Archer
  "arcane_skeleton": "Nobody said necromancy was the only magic skeletons were allowed to possess, even though its power universally gives them undeath. A careful wizard has implanted spellbound gemstones in this skeleton's skull, giving it natural catalysts, which in this case it uses to drain life essence by telekinetically yanking on foes' hair.", // Arcane Skeleton
  "ghost_knight": "In a land so deeply steeped in chaos and magic, the journey of a chivalric oath need not end in death. A knight left to die slowly in possession of his willpower may sometimes leave behind their soul as a ghost. Only upon completion of the knightly quest can the soul find its eternal rest.", // Ghost Knight
  "ghost_plunderer": "Those plunderers covetous enough to journey fruitlessly in pursuit of ultimate fortune often times become wrapped up in tall tales, the rocking of their boats on the sea lulling them into hypnotic belief in the improbable. This may explain the prevalence of ghosts aboard cursed pirate ships at sea.", // Ghost Plunderer
  "ghost_assassin": "It is not terribly uncommon for those ghosts left behind by vendettas to commune with the living, inspiring them to violent murder. What you'll find less often are ghosts, such as this one, who take killing the living upon themselves. This one has many targets, and waits for nobody's aid in efficiently dispatching them.", // Ghost Assassin
  "vindictive_ghost": "While it takes a purpose to animate as a ghost in undeath, it does not necessarily mean that the resulting ghost will remember this goal. The Vindictive Ghost has been undead a long time, and really really hates it. He wants to rest in peace. Unfortunately, his forgetfulness currently prevents him from finding fulfillment in undeath, so he has a lot of pent-up rage to take out until he remembers his ghostly task once again.", // Vindictive Ghost
  "ghost_terrifier": "This particular depraved ghost delights in nothing more than to scare the life out of those around her. She died of a heart attack brought on by sudden shock, and she lived a life of petty grudges, full of regret. Until each and every one of her chosen enemies is striken by madness, she will not rest in peace.", // Ghost Terrifier
  "ghost_bruiser": "Living in the streets of the capital city, this unfortunate soul was always called the runt of the litter. Though small, he worked long and hard on his physique and never portrayed weakness. And when he was finally killed for his involvement in crime gangs, he hadn't quite outlived his reputation a weakling yet. He had a job to finish.", // Ghost Bruiser
  "alien_mage": "When alien scouts first encountered human magic, they wondered almost immediately how their species hadn't thought of it first. The ingenius practice combined scientific observation with exactly the kind of analytical processes their brains thrived on unravelling. With human invention and alien intellect combined, future magics may soon reach new heights.", // Alien Mage
  "alien_ooze": "Little is known about the alien reproductive cycle. This ooze seems to contain an alien, as well as a fluid containing a flexible compound that can morph into other genetic makeups. Whether this is an larval stage or an adult bodily process is entirely unclear.", // Alien Ooze
  "alien_wildcat": "There is one type of fauna from the human realms that aliens instantly recognized, though their version is decidedly more purple. The whole 'nine lives' thing we say about them is the most confusing part. Do we mean eyes, they wonder? But our version only has two. Few conclusions can be drawn about the peculiar human expression.", // Alien Wildcat
  "alien_invader": "There are those more cavalier individuals among the aliens who don't let their frailer frames stop them. Even with what little technology an alien carry on them, such as the ray gun, they are more than equipped to take on the intellectually less capable residents of our world. Or at least this particular alien would say so.", // Alien Invader
  "predatory_alien": "This alien makes use of biological manipulation to greatly increase its natural offensive potential while sacrificing certain aspects of its appearance. Luckily, alien society does not value things like this, and compared to humans aliens are a lot less emotionally attached to their physical forms and lives more generally.", // Predatory Alien
  "alien_triblade": "Without some way of making up their physical disadvantage, aliens find themselves severely outmatched against humans and the forces of our world that toughened us. But by harnessing biological engineering, some aliens attempt to remedy this issue through technological means other than mechanical. Take for example the triblade and its third arm, which wields its blade by reflex alone to avoid overloading the alien's brain circuits.", // Alien Triblade
  "conjured_bonelord": "A wizard once claimed openly in a magic school that necromantic summons were lower-order for consisting only of the sum of their parts, using bone as mere golem fodder rather than constructing a cohesive creature. One reclusive necromancer, taking this personally, designed this creature with the sole purpose of defeating the arrogant wizard. It consists of no less than two thousand five hundred collected bones.", // Conjured Bonelord
  "clammering_bone_serpent": "This serpent is no serpent at all, and is instead made of a mass of smashed-together human bones found in the great bone pit beneath the foot of the endless mountains. Those humans wondering what happens to their dead when their bones leave the soil need look no further than monstrosities like this. Skeletons from beneath the ground harvest those bones constantly through magical means to fuel the pits, and in turn construct creatures such as these.", // Clammering Bone Serpent
  "wailing_revenant": "This howler of the night died from lack of sleep due to the people in her town constantly making noise, her neighbours seeming to seem up an incessent noctural racket each and every night. When her anger and deprivation turned to early demise, the unfortunate spirit began undeath fully formed and maliciously powerful. Though she has long since achieved her revenge, she has clung to undeath, her rage yet unfulfilled.", // Wailing Revenant
  "cackling_puppeteer": "The Cackling Puppeteer was born of an extremely peculiar and manipulative soul, a playmaster who put on elaborate productions to the point of sadism against his actors. There were few if any other people like him in the realms of humanity, even as theater was commonly practiced throughout in times of peace. His designs for those he knew who outlived him are as of yet unclear.", // Cackling Puppeteer
  "assault_lander": "While the alien engineers who design such devices will be among the first to explain that this is not a particularly efficient way to go about conquering another world, there is nonetheless an evergrowing demand for devices such as these coming from those parts of alien society where wealth and enthusiasm intersect. This one is equipped for combat with a neurotoxin emitter as well as a rapid-fire heavy laser cannon.", // Assault Lander
  "soundwave_shock_trooper": "One interesting physiological quirk common among aliens is their use of telepathy, which eliminates the need for hearing. Since they do not have this sense, aliens are free to weaponize sound against humans and other being vulnerable to it. So far, only a select few, such as this shock trooper, have realized the potential of doing so.", // Soundwave Shock Trooper
  "ossified_direwyrm": "In a seemingly clever bid to defeat a direwyrm armed with the element of fire, a team of wizards conspired quickly to swap its lifeforce with that of a nearby lifeless skeleton. The intensely magical creature altered the spell in its course, becoming instead an ossified but yet-living version of its former self. The party found this creature no easier to defeat, perishing quickly at its hands.", // Ossified Direwyrm
  "deadly_brain_symbiote": "Between those few learned souls in the know about both the bursters, spies of the Faceless King, and the aliens from the inter-world portal found beyond the endless mountains, this particular symbiote originating among the latter may seem eerily familiar. The difference is that the alien undergoing this ritual does so willingly, and retains all of their consciousness.", // Deadly Brain Symbiote
  "terrifying_executioner": "Little is known about the origin of the soul that possessed this disturbed mind to perform a fusion ritual with the dead. He kills silently, though his confident, steady motions and fearsomely sadistic methods suggest an underlying purpose to his streak of gruesome killing. One thing that is certain to drive this depraved half-living killer is bloodlust.", // Terrifying Executioner
  "skull_union_monarchy": "Skeletons, not content to serve the same bonelords forever, sometimes conspire to combine into larger bonepiles. This especially ambitious example resulted from hundred of thousands of selected bones, ensouled by a mass of clackling skeletons chanting around it to accept the worthiest pieces among them and reject the weak, and to rise as their new leader to march against the forces of the living.", // Skull-Union Monarchy
  "tally_ho_laser_squad": "Aliens don't do things exactly like us humans, but just look at them for a second. I honestly think they're kind of getting the spirit of it. Whatever points they lose for accuracy, I say they win back for effort by showing up ready to fight on our terms.", // Tally-Ho Laser Squad
  "revenant_trio": "What's worse than being haunted by a ghost? How about a vindictive trio of them. One of their friends was brought fresh to the afterlife just so he could join the squad, to ensure that the right combination of ghostly professionals is present to accomplish their mission.", // Revenant Trio

  // ---- Hidden Avatars ----
  "western_wind_avatar": "When glory and honour bored the lancer, he sought secretly and for years to transcend mere victory and perfect a technique that others would hail as a revolution in lancing. Struck by a metaphorical wall, his only choice was to challenge the dragon of the Western Winds to see his vision to fruition. And such was his dedication that the mount accepted its rider after little struggle, in tribute to his immense skill.", // Western Wind Avatar
  "crimson_dusk_avatar": "Inspired by the glaring red of the sky as the sun set one dusk, the fighter asked himself how one destined to kill for all his days could be afforded such beauty. As his mind reached for it with intensity and desire, the ritual became complete. And just as the mouth of the great serpent would have closed around him, a reflexive tug of his chain whip strangled it around the neck. Kicking free and swinging away, he found himself atop his new mount.", // Crimson Dusk Avatar
  "endothermic_geo_vent_avatar": "Aliens quickly took to human magic when they first discovered it, finding the concrete rules simple to grasp. For example, to become an avatar, perform the ritual. Then, subdue and mount the summoned spirit beast before it can devour you. For example- wait, you're supposed to pick a sky phenomenon. Endothermic? So their land is colder on the ins-? AHHH! Run. Just run. I don't know what that damned thing is.", // Endothermic Geo-Vent Avatar
  "cruel_maelstrom_avatar": "She bested the great crow-roc of the cruel maelstrom by wresting the very lightning powers it wielded away with her superior control. Such is her indomitable control over the forces of the storm, which she wields without mercy. Weaklings who approach without care find a strange calm in breathlessness, hardly feeling a thing as they are reduced to carrion.", // Cruel Maelstrom Avatar

  // ---- Tokens ----
  "obstructing_wall": "Gets in the way of doing just about anything.", // Obstructing Wall
  "raging_bonfire": "Steer clear of the rage or it'll all be taken out on you.", // Raging Bonfire
  "toadstool": "A common mushroom of an uncommon size.", // Toadstool
  "freak": "This unfortunate creature is the brainchild of an uncaring creator, building it for one purpose alone. It cannot think or feel.", // Freak
  "apparition": "A long-dead soul forgotten by all but one person, it doesn't know that the one it faithfully protects is also long-dead.", // Apparition
};
